<article class="work">
  <p>
    Venice Time Machine is a major research undertaking led by EPFL's DHLab. The
    project aims to transform centuries of archives into data, then network that
    data to reconstruct the past using algorithms.
  </p>
  <p>
    Facing the need to provide access to already-digitized data and to bring
    several research projects together into a unified interface, DHLab brought
    me on to explore different interface concepts.
  </p>
  <p>Avec <a href="https://www.laurentbolli.com">Laurent Bolli</a></p>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-Browse.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        A spatio-temporal browser inspired by audiovisual sequencers.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <div class="detail-crop">
        <img src="images/VTM-Browse-CloseUp.jpg" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Each event is represented by a <em>diamond</em>. In the
        <em>sequencer</em> (Timeline), the length of the
        <em>diamond</em> corresponds to a duration in time.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-BrowseCadastre.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        The map view allows different geographic representations to be layered
        (historical maps, aerial or satellite views, photogrammetry).
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <div class="detail-crop">
        <img src="images/VTM-Blank-and-Error-states.jpg" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>Messages for empty states or errors.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <div class="detail-crop">
        <img src="images/VTM-Map-Markers.svg" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>Geographic markers</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-Search-Home.jpg" />
      <figcaption>The homepage contains only a search field.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-Search-Tips.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        Examples of complex searches are available directly within the
        interface.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <div class="detail-crop">
        <img src="images/VTM-Search-Results-CloseUp.jpg" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Detail of the results page. A histogram shows the density of results
        spread out over time.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-Search-Results.jpg" />
      <figcaption>Search results page</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-Document-Viewer.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        The document viewer lets you consult sources in their original context.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-Identity-Symbol.svg" />
      <div class="detail-crop bg-vtm-violet">
        <img src="images/VTM-Identity-Logo.svg" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        The symbol refers simultaneously to the <i>diamonds</i> that represent
        events, and to the Time Machine's internal geographic coordinate system.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/VTM-TimeMachineEU.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        Website promoting the project's expansion to the European level.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</article>

